from the gales and tides, is the unity from which Rinascita was born, and is ascension for our souls.\n \nThe Order's doctrines are thus: <b>“Salvation,\" \"Ascension,\" and \"Unity.\"</b>\n- Salvation: By the grace of the Sentinel, Their followers must deliver salvation to others. Nary are we blind to injustice or suffering. We labor to save others from sin. To the wicked, the Order provides salvation, and for the unrepentant, may we exact penitence.\n- Ascension: To find salvation is to seek ascension. Members of the Order will not indulge Their favor in idle pleasures or desires. All must elevate their spirit through self-discipline or risk sinking into the abyss.\n- Unity: After granting us Their representation on earth, Sentinel Imperator left Rinascita in our care. Members of the Order are \"brothers and sisters,\" who unite people of faith, regardless of origin or background. Only as one can we fortify ourselves from the perils of the deep sea.\n \nThe first Primus, Napoli the Second, received a prophecy from the Sentinel: in a distant future, a <b>\"Last Wave\"</b> shall engulf the earth. Those saved must \"breathe,\" to \"ascend\" in \"unity\" on new land, just as we once answered the Sentinel's call and made landfall on Rinascita.\n \n3. Is there evidence to support the doctrine of the Order?\n \nTheology is a science humanity has not yet fully understood in theory or practice. The Sentinel guides civilization, and we trust Their word. Throughout the generations, the Order has established the following philosophical precepts.\n \nExcerpts from The Philosophy of the Order: Sacred Knowledge (Volume 1: Water):\n \nOn Origin: Genesis in \"Water.\"\nIn nature \"Water\" is infinite as it is universal.\nIn the beginning, Sentinel Imperator \"split\" this world, once a formless ocean, into the realm of land and sea.\n \nOn Motion: Movement through \"Water.\"\nThe motion of \"Water\" heats and cools, wets and dries the realm of land. From water, all life was created in the \"First Wave\" and will end in the \"Last Wave.\"\n \nOn Revelations: Refractions of \"Water.\"\nMan's image reflected by \"Water\" is a strange reality unto himself. So too applies to all reality when water refracts the world unto the Sonoro Sphere.\n \nThrough reforms by successive Primuses, we have come to emphasize the scientific and practical application of our philosophical understanding. Readers may visit Arito Well in the Square of Liberty to experience the mysteries of \"water divination\": toss a coin into the well, make a heartfelt wish, and answers you shall receive.\n \nWe would be greatly honored if this Codex engenders interest in the Sentinel's teachings, and we welcome all to the Order's library, where supplementary literature is available to borrow.\n \nWhile words are a paltry means to express the Sentinel's grand purpose, we nonetheless hope to have adequately conveyed fractions of divine essence. Let miracles recorded in the Codex be \"symbols\" of infinite, communicable power. Through narratives of common understanding, we envision a world of unwavering faith. Even as the Lament threatens to return, we reaffirm our place and purpose.\n \nWe pray that believers and non-believers alike will view the text herein as an invitation for communion and reflection. May these words offer insight to us all.\n\nLost as we are in the oceans of this earthly realm, there is more than one way to rise. Cling to light and goodness, and even in the blackest waters, you shall find your ship.",
   "InfoDisplay_311000010_Title": "<i>Codex of the Deep: Preface (137th Edition)</i>",
   "InfoDisplay_311000011_Text": "(Drums beat solemnly as Fleurdelys, Brand, and other Acolytes enter, each carrying relics.)\n\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: Lo, the Dark Tide hath momentarily receded, granting Rinascita a fleeting respite. I doth thank each of you for your unwavering commitment through these trying days.\n\n<b>Brand</b>: My lady, you honor us beyond measure. We serve not only thee but also the Sentinel. When Rinascita hangeth by a thread, how could we place our own survival above our sacred duty? Besides, thou didst stand beside us, taking up arms and leading us to face the Dark Tide, endured grievous wounds without faltering. Thou art the very embodiment of the purity and devotion of an Acolyte, and of the courage and valor of a warrior. Inspired by thy fortitude, we are prepared to offer our lives without hesitation.\n\n<b>Brand</b>: Yet the glimmer of light emerged in the north was swiftly quenched by the merciless Dark Tide, which surged back like a ravenous beast, devouring our lands. Our soldiers fought valiantly, only to be swept away by the relentless onslaught. Though the tide hath withdrawn for now, its return is as certain as fate itself. I fear that, over time, our strength may falter…\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: …Perchance there remains a glimmer of hope.\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: Not long ago, as I lay unconscious from my wounds, I was trapped in a relentless nightmare for three days and nights, lost in darkness without end. But in the depths of that abyss, a faint light didst appear—They spoke unto me. Their words of boundless mercy soothed my scarred soul and awakened me. They revealed that the wound upon Their own divine body fuelleth the Dark Tide, and only through a shared bond of strength could this wound be healed. I have been called to journey eastward, to reach the high heavens in the mist, and thus break the curse of the Dark Tide.\n\n<b>Brand</b>: Praise be to Sentinel Imperator! My lady, if this oracle is true, and thou hast shared thy strength with the Sentinel… could it be that the prophesied Enlightened One hath already walked among us?\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: I dare not presume such things. When I received this divine calling and assumed my role, the Sentinel didst not reveal the truth of the Enlightened One unto me.\n\n<b>Brand</b>: But my lady, thou hast wrought countless miracles, lifting our people from suffering and offering prayers on their behalf. To us, thou art the Blessed Maiden. In our eyes, thou art no less than the Enlightened One.\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: Be that as it may, I have my duty to the Sentinel. Now that I know the path to Their throne, it falls upon me to stop the curse at its very root, for Rinascita cannot bear further sacrifice.\n\n<b>Brand</b>: Indeed! Guards, prepare to escort the lady!\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: Nay, please stay. The Dark Tide still looms in the north, and the guards are better placed to protect the people than to accompany me.\n\n<b>Brand</b>: But...\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: This is my path to walk alone, as entrusted to me by the Sentinel. This journey may well be my last. If I do not return, it will be thy duty to tend the Order's affairs.\n\n(Acolytes begin to weep softly in the background.)\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: Grieve not. This is the path for which I was chosen. Should fates be kind, the Dark Tide will soon vanish, and Rinascita will flourish once more. When that day comes, remember me in joyful songs rather than somber laments. I verily believe the Sentinel wouldst wish the same.. (smiles warmly)\n\n<b>Brand</b>: As thou dost wish, my lady. If thou art to travel east, Priest Fenrico is stationed there with a detachment of the guard. He may be able to aid thee.\n\n<b>Fleurdelys</b>: Behold, dawn breaketh anew. No matter how long the night, the daylight cometh. Though our path be fraught with tears, we shall walk it with songs and courage. This is Rinascita's greatest treasure and humanity's strongest shield—our unbroken will, unwavering faith, and unquenchable hope! (exits)\n\n<b>Brand</b>: May thy sword be blessed, to calm storms and sever the tides! (exits)\n\n<i>To Be Continued</i>\n\nAuthor's Note:\nThis work is incomplete, a humble draft that needs further refinement. According to historical records, the Dark Tide ended shortly after the Blessed Maiden set out. Yet, the Blessed Maiden herself… left us forever, returning to the divine embrace. It is said that she held back the Dark Tide through her martyrdom, using the very last of her strength.\nThese fragments of history inspire endless curiosity: Who, truly, was the Enlightened One? Was the Blessed Maiden indeed the Enlightened One the prophecy suggested? What happened after her departure? Do the legendary high heavens exist? And what could have inflicted such a wound upon the Sentinel that even They could not heal? These mysteries remain unanswered.\nAs all stories are but interpretations, this is merely one version. Should anyone possess further historical insights, I welcome your critique and guidance. My gratitude in advance.",
   "InfoDisplay_311000011_Title": "<b>The Martyrdom of Blessed Fleurdelys (Unfinished) Act III, Scene 1</b>",
